{
  "engine": "bpjs/monthly-contributions",
  "rateSet": "structural-fiction-v1",
  "_readme": [
    "Structural vectors (ADR-0018 §3): rate-independent logic only, computed against the",
    "deliberately fictional BPJS section of structural-fiction-v1.ts — rates in 10%-steps,",
    "caps on round numbers, a JP age ceiling of 100, a rounding unit of 1000. Nothing here",
    "is or resembles Indonesian regulation.",
    "What these pin: the §4.3 resolution ladder's order, floor_applies selection per row,",
    "per-program caps binding differently in one run, the JP ceiling deriving from birthDate,",
    "the per-program-per-payer month credit, employer premiums classified regular vs",
    "non_taxable, the deductible JHT+JP pair, the dependent surcharge, and half-up rounding",
    "to the unit.",
    "A failing vector is a code defect until a human re-verifies it and records why it",
    "changed; a vector is never edited to make a test pass (testing-strategy §6.1).",
    "Input mirrors BpjsInput minus `parameters` (injected by the runner from the declared",
    "rateSet). Expected omits `trace` — the runner asserts trace completeness structurally."
  ],
